{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6c9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e75-bbc6-7500-a9cb-f70149b63e89"},"sequence":447,"recorded_at":1780531400000889,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"5c231d3a-fdb3-439c-92eb-3636806f93dd"},"task_id":"5c231d3a-fdb3-439c-92eb-3636806f93dd","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"5c231d3a-fdb3-439c-92eb-3636806f93dd","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1949 line(s) above)\n1950|why `unmeasured` is refused rather than admitted: the gate reports that it could\n1951|not measure the section instead of inferring that there was nothing to measure.\n1952|And the gap-quality check is a tightening rather than a proof - a sentence that\n1953|names both its section and its production declaration and still says nothing\n1954|useful is admitted, and the gate cannot decide otherwise.\n1955|\n1956|### Measured coverage of this repository\n1957|\n1958|`tracecheck` prints the ratio it measured rather than a sentence about it:\n1959|\n1960|```text\n1961|section coverage: bindings=49 full=1 partial=3 sliver=1 unevidenced=41 unmeasured=3 unowned=2 clauses_discharged=17/403\n1962|```\n1963|\n1964|Forty-nine section bindings discharge 17 of the 403 normative clauses their\n1965|sections carry. One binding is `full` (Section 6.2, whose single clause is the\n1966|native-Windows `conpty` requirement, discharged by\n1967|`TestEveryPinnedReaderHasPositiveNativeWindowsAndWSL2Lanes`), three are\n1968|`partial` (Section 14.2 at 8/9, bound to\n1969|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult), whose undischarged clause `14.2#6`\n1970|is the process exit status this repository has no binary to produce; and\n1971|Section 15.1 at 5/7 and Section 15.3 at 2/3, both bound to\n1972|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror); the three undischarged clauses there are\n1973|the RPC hello obligation `15.1#5`, the bootstrap-row sentence `15.1#6` that\n1974|binds the provider plugin rather than the host, and the hello-key and\n1975|TerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository builds no RPC\n1976|hello frame, no provider plugin, and no TerminalBackend capability set), one is\n1977|`sliver` (Section 10.3, whose chunk offset invariant is\n1978|enforced by `validateBlobDescriptor` while its two receiver clauses have no\n1979|implementation), three are `unmeasured` (Sections 7.3, 13.14.5 and 15.2, each of\n1980|which carries a gap saying why the scanner measures zero and what is missing),\n1981|and forty-one are `unevidenced`. Two sections are recorded unowned.\n1982|Assigned-scope admission therefore succeeds today for `-section 6.2` and\n1983|nothing else; every other assignment is refused with its ratio and its gap.\n1984|A `partial` binding is refused by assigned-scope admission exactly like an\n1985|`unevidenced` one: admission requires `full`.\n1986|\n1987|One admitted binding out of forty-nine is a thin positive arm, and it is\n1988|disclosed here rather than hidden: without Section 6.2 the admit path would only\n1989|ever be exercised synthetically.\n1990|\n1991|That is a disclosure of the shipped state, not a target that was met.\n1992|`TestRunRefusesEveryAssignedSectionThatOnlySlivers` and\n1993|`TestVerifyAssignedSectionsRefusesEveryBindingThatOnlySlivers` pin every failing\n1994|binding with its exact measured ratio, so a section that becomes covered has to\n1995|leave those tables deliberately. Five further gaps the disclosure surfaced:\n1996|Section 15.2's code-to-exit registry is implemented in\n1997|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) and checked row by row, and\n1998|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult) now maps a failure to that exact\n1999|process status through `Emit` and `ExitStatus`, but nothing in the tree calls\n(more lines below)"}}}
