{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6cf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e75-bbc6-7500-a9cb-f70149b63e89"},"sequence":450,"recorded_at":1780531400000895,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a8267f27-f83c-4f74-8515-f1a7f75284ca"},"task_id":"a8267f27-f83c-4f74-8515-f1a7f75284ca","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a8267f27-f83c-4f74-8515-f1a7f75284ca","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-17-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"2xdt8t\\\\|required_capabilities\\\\|platform lane minimum\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head -20; echo ===; ls internal/traceability/; echo ===; grep -n \\\"6.2\\\" internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json | head\",\n  \"description\": \"Find logbook entry and ownership registry\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"10:- SCOPE: new `internal/terminalbackend/` (registry, canonical IDs, version tuples, trust, duplicate/drift refusal, restore binding, §7.A descriptor check), `internal/config/validation.go` wiring, new `internal/config/terminal_registry_wiring_test.go`. TASK-260830-2xdt8t, spec v0.5.0 §4.B, §4.1, §6.5, §7.A. Signed commit on story branch, worktree clean, not pushed.\\n11:- DECISION (finding 1): `required_capabilities` keeps its empty default. SPEC.md:2585 (\\\"default platform lane minimum\\\") is the sole occurrence of the phrase in the 12,665-line SPEC; no per-platform minimum set is enumerated anywhere, so implementing one would invent a constraint. Empty enables nothing per SPEC.md:2604-2605 (\\\"Policy may further restrict capabilities/transports but cannot enable an unsupported claim\\\"); per-operation capability dependencies (§4.C/§4.D) still gate activation. No code change.\\n222:- FINDING: the disclosure surfaced two more of the same shape that no audit had named. `section:17.2`'s single clause is an unknown-event *reader* obligation while its binding names the Configuration *writer* `EncodeCurrent`; `section:2.1`'s single clause is a replica runtime obligation nothing here implements. §6.5 kept its binding but its gap names a real defect: SPEC.md:2585 requires `required_capabilities` to default to the platform lane minimum, and `internal/config/validation.go:670` accepts only an empty default.\\n===\\ncmd\\nownership.v0.5.0.json\\nreadme_figures_pin_test.go\\ntraceability_test.go\\ntraceability.go\\n===\\n9:    \\\"document_sha256\\\": \\\"562546d240f0fa3e71b47e6359a002f9892c0efd97e19eb55917527552ac484a\\\"\\n2501:        \\\"section:6.2\\\"\\n2513:          \\\"id\\\": \\\"6.2#1\\\",\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 1668,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 417,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
