ligation `15.1#5`, the bootstrap-row sentence `15.1#6` that\n1974|binds the provider plugin rather than the host, and the hello-key and\n1975|TerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository builds no RPC\n1976|hello frame, no provider plugin, and no TerminalBackend capability set), one is\n1977|`sliver` (Section 10.3, whose chunk offset invariant is\n1978|enforced by `validateBlobDescriptor` while its two receiver clauses have no\n1979|implementation), three are `unmeasured` (Sections 7.3, 13.14.5 and 15.2, each of\n1980|which carries a gap saying why the scanner measures zero and what is missing),\n1981|and forty-one are `unevidenced`. Two sections are recorded unowned.\n1982|Assigned-scope admission therefore succeeds today for `-section 6.2` and\n1983|nothing else; every other assignment is refused with its ratio and its gap.\n1984|A `partial` binding is refused by assigned-scope admission exactly like an\n1985|`unevidenced` one: admission requires `full`.\n1986|\n1987|One admitted binding out of forty-nine is a thin positive arm, and it is\n1988|disclosed here rather than hidden: without Section 6.2 the admit path would only\n1989|ever be exercised synthetically.\n1990|\n1991|That is a disclosure of the shipped state, not a target that was met.\n1992|`TestRunRefusesEveryAssignedSectionThatOnlySlivers` and\n1993|`TestVerifyAssignedSectionsRefusesEveryBindingThatOnlySlivers` pin every failing\n1994|binding with its exact measured ratio, so a section that becomes covered has to\n1995|leave those tables deliberately. Five further gaps the disclosure surfaced:\n1996|Section 15.2's code-to-exit registry is implemented in\n1997|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) and checked row by row, and\n1998|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult) now maps a failure to that exact\n1999|process status through `Emit` and `ExitStatus`, but nothing in the tree calls\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e75-bbc6-7500-a9cb-f70149b63e89"},"sequence":453,"recorded_at":1780531400000901,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c"},"call_id":"call_01a06e76cdbd7113a69717f0fc174d12","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-17-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"2xdt8t\\\\|required_capabilities\\\\|platform lane minimum\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head -20; echo ===; ls internal/traceability/; echo ===; grep -n \\\"6.2\\\" internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json | head\",\n  \"description\": \"Find logbook entry and ownership registry\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"10:- SCOPE: new `internal/terminalbackend/` (registry, canonical IDs, version tuples, trust, duplicate/drift refusal, restore binding, §7.A descriptor check), `internal/config/validation.go` wiring, new `internal/config/terminal_registry_wiring_test.go`. TASK-260830-2xdt8t, spec v0.5.0 §4.B, §4.1, §6.5, §7.A. Signed commit on story branch, worktree clean, not pushed.\\n11:- DECISION (finding 1): `required_capabilities` keeps its empty default. SPEC.md:2585 (\\\"default platform lane minimum\\\") is the sole occurrence of the phrase in the 12,665-line SPEC; no per-platform minimum set is enumerated anywhere, so implementing one would invent a constraint. Empty enables nothing per SPEC.md:2604-2605 (\\\"Policy may further restrict capabilities/transports but cannot enable an unsupported claim\\\"); per-operation capability dependencies (§4.C/§4.D) still gate activation. No code change.\\n222:- FINDING: the disclosure surfaced two more of the same shape that no audit had named. `section:17.2`'s single clause is an unknown-event *reader* obligation while its binding names the Configuration *writer* `EncodeCurrent`; `section:2.1`'s single clause is a replica runtime obligation nothing here implements. §6.5 kept its binding but its gap names a real defect: SPEC.md:2585 requires `required_capabilities` to default to the platform lane minimum, and `internal/config/validation.go:670` accepts only an empty default.\\n===\\ncmd\\nownership.v0.5.0.json\\nreadme_figures_pin_test.go\\ntraceability_test.go\\ntraceability.go\\n===\\n9:    \\\"document_sha256\\\": \\\"562546d240f0fa3e71b47e6359a002f9892c0efd97e19eb55917527552ac484a\\\"\\n2501:        \\\"section:6.2\\\"\\n2513:          \\\"id\\\": \\\"6.2#1\\\",\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 1668,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 417,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
