{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd3d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e75-bbc6-7500-a9cb-f70149b63e89"},"sequence":1273,"recorded_at":1780531400002541,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"e79dd724-59fd-4830-9402-f9edd426b0ca"},"task_id":"e79dd724-59fd-4830-9402-f9edd426b0ca","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"e79dd724-59fd-4830-9402-f9edd426b0ca","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-04\n-\n-### 2147 — Terminal backend registry: the two board-disclosed findings decided without inventing constraints\n+## 2026-09-04\n+\n+### 2210 — Terminal backend registry rework: aliasing bypass closed, four unmeasured domains measured\n+\n+- SCOPE: rework of TASK-260830-2xdt8t after CHANGES REQUESTED (five blocking findings F1–F5). Production: `internal/terminalbackend` clones slices on ingress (`New` per-builtin copy, `RegisterExternal` store copy) and egress (`Resolve` return copy). No new refusal sites.\n+- F1: `Resolve` returned the struct by value with shared backing arrays, `RegisterExternal` stored the caller record verbatim, `New` shared one protocol array across both built-ins — an in-place mutation converted drift into `terminal_backend_ambiguous` and the registry adopted the change. Pinned by `TestRegistryCopiesSlicesAcrossItsBoundary` (four subtests, incl. the end-to-end duplicate-instead-of-drift bypass).\n+- F2: drift table gains same-length cases (`[\"1.0.0\"]→[\"1.1.0\"]`, `[linux]→[macos]`); the length-changing cases alone left the member loops deletable.\n+- F3: generation-bound test rewritten with EQUAL generations on both sides (1 and 256 admitted; 0 and 257 refused); mismatch arm split into `TestCheckProviderDescriptorGenerationMismatch`. The old test proved the inequality, not the bound.\n+- F4: `validatePlatforms` fully narrowed (dup/empty/unknown/5-list, with the 5-list asserting the `platforms bound` clause since any 5-list over the 4-member vocabulary also fails a later rule); protocol `[1..32]` bound pinned with 33 distinct sorted members plus 32-member admission; `DigestFile` FIFO case pins the `IsRegular` guard (the directory case is EISDIR-confounded); trust-loop `ParseID` pinned against deletion by the `INVALID_ID` wiring case.\n+- EQUIVALENT MUTANTS (documented, not covered): reverting the trust-loop `ParseID` to the previous local pattern is behavior-identical — same refusal set, intentionally non-distinguishing clause, `ax.` difference subsumed by the `HasPrefix` line two statements later. `parseKind`'s vocabulary arm and the digest-must-be-null arm are unreachable through current entry points (external-kind gate precedes validation with `Untrusted`, pinned by `TestRegisterExternalRefusesUnknownKindAsUntrusted`); measured white-box in `internal_pin_test.go` with the reachability bound stated.\n+- F5: `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` registered in `config-versioned-readers`; ownership projection digest re-pinned; README discharge prose names both arms. No figure moved (74 cases, 17/403).\n+- EVIDENCE: `TASK-260830-2xdt8t_rework-verification.md` (board outcome artifact) with the mutation re-run ratio.\n+\n+### 2147 — Terminal backend registry: the two board-disclosed findings decided without inventing constraints\n"}}}
