{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d091","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e75-bbc6-7500-a9cb-f70149b63e89"},"sequence":1699,"recorded_at":1780531400003393,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e2efeb9-af88-4b92-82e3-c4ef7a43be2c"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Rework of TASK-260830-2xdt8t is ready for review (board status `to-review`, checklist 15/15).\n\nWhat changed, on signed commit `9e31f14` above reviewed `b5cf5b5`, worktree clean, not pushed:\n\n- **F1 (drift gate bypass) fixed**: `New`, `RegisterExternal`, and `Resolve` now deep-copy slices on ingress and egress, matching the existing `catalog`/`specpin`/`config` clone convention. Pinned by `TestRegistryCopiesSlicesAcrossItsBoundary`, including the end-to-end drift-reported-as-duplicate bypass.\n- **F2**: same-length drift cases (`1.0.0→1.1.0`, `[linux]→[macos]`) so the member loops, not just length guards, are exercised.\n- **F3**: generation-bound test rewritten with equal generations on both sides (1 and 256 admitted; 0 and 257 refused); mismatch arm split out.\n- **F4**: all guard domains narrowed — platform violations with clause assertions, 33-distinct/32-admission protocol bound, FIFO pin for `DigestFile`, malformed-trust-ID wiring case; white-box pins for entry-unreachable arms. Targeted mutation re-run: 13/13 killed, each confirmed present, sources restored. Two declared equivalents with contract reasons: M28-revert (behavior-identical at this call site) and the unreachable-arm guards.\n- **F5**: §6.2 negative arm registered in `config-versioned-readers`, projection digest re-pinned, README names both arms; figures unmoved (74 cases, 17/403). D1 LOGBOOK restated as a stated bound, 2604-2605 reasoning withdrawn.\n\nEvidence: `go test ./...` green (14 packages, exit 0), `go vet` clean, `gofmt` clean, `tracecheck` and `-section 6.2` green; outcome artifact `TASK-260830-2xdt8t_rework-verification.md` attached to the board.\n\nOne coordination note for review: the ownership-JSON digest re-pin may need merge-order recomputation if the parallel story moves that digest first — flagged in the artifact.","reason":null}}
